{"timestamp":1774880888179,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"f1ef5520-7e25-4f2e-9ff6-68a1a06d53ac","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_018qxeKC6NfoKLu8BFofw3kp","payload":{"session_id":"f1ef5520-7e25-4f2e-9ff6-68a1a06d53ac","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-f32e4400/f1ef5520-7e25-4f2e-9ff6-68a1a06d53ac.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/f32e4400","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"find /Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/f32e4400 -name \"DECISIONS.md\" 2>/dev/null | head -5","description":"Find DECISIONS.md files"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_018qxeKC6NfoKLu8BFofw3kp"}}
{"timestamp":1774880975796,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"f1ef5520-7e25-4f2e-9ff6-68a1a06d53ac","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LbybMQKyZ9YyAgwp5nSUwU","payload":{"session_id":"f1ef5520-7e25-4f2e-9ff6-68a1a06d53ac","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-f32e4400/f1ef5520-7e25-4f2e-9ff6-68a1a06d53ac.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/f32e4400","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/f32e4400/.pinata/specs/issue-11-adw-f32e4400-sdlc_planner-prevent-duplicate-fragment-title-clone.md","content":"# Plan: Prevent Duplicate Fragment Title for Cloned Cards in M@S Studio\n\n## Summary\nWhen a user clones a card in M@S Studio, the clone dialog pre-displays the original fragment's title but the internal `titleClone` state starts empty, so confirming without editing leaves the copy with the same title. This plan adds a `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` method to `MasRepository` that appends an incrementing `-N` suffix when a title collision is detected against the in-memory fragment list, and wires `showClone()` to initialize `titleClone` with the computed unique title before the dialog opens.\n\n## Task Description\n- Add `generateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle)` to `MasRepository` that:\n  - Reads existing titles from `Store.fragments.list.data` (path-scoped to current view)\n  - If `baseTitle` is already taken, strips any trailing `-N` suffix to get a root, then returns the first `root-N` not present\n- Fix `showClone()` in `MasFragmentEditor` to call the new method and store the result in `this.titleClone`\n- Update the clone dialog template to bind `value` to `this.titleClone` instead of `this.fragment.title`\n- Reset `titleClone` to `''` in `cancelClone()`\n- Add unit tests for `generateUniqueFragmentTitle`\n\n## Relevant Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `studio/src/mas-repository.js` | Add `generateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle)` method |\n| `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js` | Modify `showClone()`, clone dialog template, `cancelClone()` |\n| `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` | Add unit tests for the new method |\n\n## Step by Step Tasks\n\n### 1. Add `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` to `MasRepository`\n\nIn `studio/src/mas-repository.js`, add the following method to the `MasRepository` class (e.g., right before `copyFragment`):\n\n```js\n/**\n * Returns a unique fragment title by appending a numeric suffix if a fragment\n * with the same title already exists in the current in-memory list.\n * Uniqueness is scoped to the currently-loaded tag path (whatever is in Store.fragments.list.data).\n *\n * Examples:\n *   'lucy-card'   (exists) \u2192 'lucy-card-1'\n *   'lucy-card-1' (exists, 'lucy-card' also exists) \u2192 'lucy-card-2'\n *\n * @param {string} baseTitle - The desired title (typically the title of the fragment being cloned)\n * @returns {string} A title guaranteed not to collide with any title in the in-memory list\n */\ngenerateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle) {\n    const existingTitles = new Set(\n        (Store.fragments.list.data.get() || [])\n            .map((store) => store.get()?.title)\n            .filter(Boolean),\n    );\n\n    if (!existingTitles.has(baseTitle)) return baseTitle;\n\n    // Strip trailing -N suffix to get the root title\n    const suffixMatch = baseTitle.match(/^(.*)-(\\d+)$/);\n    const rootTitle = suffixMatch ? suffixMatch[1] : baseTitle;\n\n    let n = 1;\n    while (existingTitles.has(`${rootTitle}-${n}`)) {\n        n += 1;\n    }\n    return `${rootTitle}-${n}`;\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Initialize `titleClone` with a unique title in `showClone()`\n\nIn `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`, update `showClone()`:\n\n**Before:**\n```js\nasync showClone() {\n    if (Store.editor.hasChanges) {\n        const confirmed = await this.promptDiscardChanges();\n        if (!confirmed) return;\n    }\n    this.showCloneDialog = true;\n    Store.showCloneDialog.set(true);\n}\n```\n\n**After:**\n```js\nasync showClone() {\n    if (Store.editor.hasChanges) {\n        const confirmed = await this.promptDiscardChanges();\n        if (!confirmed) return;\n    }\n    this.titleClone = this.repository.generateUniqueFragmentTitle(this.fragment.title);\n    this.showCloneDialog = true;\n    Store.showCloneDialog.set(true);\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Bind clone dialog title input to `this.titleClone`\n\nIn `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`, update the `cloneConfirmationDialog` getter template \u2014 change the `sp-textfield` `value` binding:\n\n**Before:**\n```js\nvalue=\"${this.fragment.title}\"\n```\n\n**After:**\n```js\nvalue=\"${this.titleClone}\"\n```\n\n### 4. Reset `titleClone` in `cancelClone()`\n\nIn `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`, update `cancelClone()`:\n\n**Before:**\n```js\ncancelClone() {\n    this.showCloneDialog = false;\n    Store.showCloneDialog.set(false);\n    this.tagsClone = [];\n    this.osiClone = null;\n}\n```\n\n**After:**\n```js\ncancelClone() {\n    this.showCloneDialog = false;\n    Store.showCloneDialog.set(false);\n    this.tagsClone = [];\n    this.osiClone = null;\n    this.titleClone = '';\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Add unit tests in `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js`\n\nAdd a new `describe` block for `generateUniqueFragmentTitle`:\n\n```js\ndescribe('MasRepository#generateUniqueFragmentTitle', () => {\n    let sandbox;\n    let repository;\n\n    beforeEach(() => {\n        sandbox = sinon.createSandbox();\n        repository = Object.create(MasRepository.prototype);\n    });\n\n    afterEach(() => {\n        sandbox.restore();\n        Store.fragments.list.data.set([]);\n    });\n\n    function makeStore(title) {\n        return { get: () => ({ title }) };\n    }\n\n    it('returns the base title unchanged when no collision exists', () => {\n        Store.fragments.list.data.set([makeStore('other-card')]);\n        expect(repository.generateUniqueFragmentTitle('lucy-card')).to.equal('lucy-card');\n    });\n\n    it('appends -1 when the base title already exists', () => {\n        Store.fragments.list.data.set([makeStore('lucy-card')]);\n        expect(repository.generateUniqueFragmentTitle('lucy-card')).to.equal('lucy-card-1');\n    });\n\n    it('increments suffix beyond -1 when -1 also exists', () => {\n        Store.fragments.list.data.set([makeStore('lucy-card'), makeStore('lucy-card-1')]);\n        expect(repository.generateUniqueFragmentTitle('lucy-card')).to.equal('lucy-card-2');\n    });\n\n    it('strips existing suffix and increments when cloning a -N card', () => {\n        Store.fragments.list.data.set([makeStore('lucy-card'), makeStore('lucy-card-1')]);\n        expect(repository.generateUniqueFragmentTitle('lucy-card-1')).to.equal('lucy-card-2');\n    });\n\n    it('handles an empty fragment list gracefully', () => {\n        Store.fragments.list.data.set([]);\n        expect(repository.generateUniqueFragmentTitle('my-card')).to.equal('my-card');\n    });\n});\n```\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Cloning a card whose Fragment Title already exists in the current path produces a clone titled `<base>-1`\n- [ ] If `<base>-1` also exists, the clone is titled `<base>-2`, and so on\n- [ ] Cloning a card named `<base>-N` generates `<base>-(N+1)` (or the next available suffix)\n- [ ] Cloning a card whose Fragment Title is unique returns the title unchanged (no suffix added)\n- [ ] The original card's Fragment Title is not modified\n- [ ] Manual edits in the clone dialog are not blocked \u2014 the user may change the pre-filled title freely\n- [ ] `cancelClone()` resets `titleClone` to `''` so stale values don't persist on re-open\n\n## Validation Commands\n\n- `node --check studio/src/mas-repository.js`\n- `node --check studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`\n- `node --check studio/test/mas-repository.test.js`\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LbybMQKyZ9YyAgwp5nSUwU"}}
